     }
    },
    {
     "id": "note",
     "set": {
      "text": "size 2: counter-model at try 7 of 16",
      "tone": "accent"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "Check the hypothesis in that world: element 0 has P, element 1 has Q, so every element has P or Q. ∀x(P(x) ∨ Q(x)) is T.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "t2",
     "set": {
      "highlight": [
       [
        1,
        3
       ],
       [
        2,
        3
       ]
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "note",
     "set": {
      "text": "hypothesis ∀x(P ∨ Q): T",
      "tone": "success"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "Check the conclusion: P fails at 1 and Q fails at 0, so ∀x P(x) and ∀x Q(x) are both F, and so is their disjunction.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "t2",
     "set": {
      "highlight": [
       [
        2,
        1
       ],
       [
        1,
        2
       ]
